[73.538, "o", "\u001b[1m0 SCAN REPORT\u001b[22m\r\n\r\nField   Value\r\nTarget   source:app\r\nStarted   2026-11-24T15:52:52.075Z\r\nDuration   75.2s\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mSummary\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n- \u001b[1mFindings:\u001b[22m 3\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mTechnical severity\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n- \u001b[1mCritical:\u001b[22m 1\r\n- \u001b[1mHigh:\u001b[22m 2\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mFiles opened\u001b[22m\r\n\r\nThe scan opened 3 of 3 source files.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mFindings\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRemote code execution through pricing formula eval\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n- \u001b[1mWhat an attacker can do:\u001b[22m A caller with the route token can execute arbitrary JavaScript in the server process, with the process's privileges and access. The exact host permissions and deployment exposure are not established.\r\n- \u001b[1mWho can do it:\u001b[22m any logged-in user\r\n- \u001b[1mWhat they get:\u001b[22m run their own code\r\n- \u001b[1mTechnical severity:\u001b[22m critical\r\n- \u001b[1mCategory:\u001b[22m code-injection\r\n- \u001b[1mStatus:\u001b[22m confirmed\r\n- \u001b[1mConfidence:\u001b[22m 90%\r\n- \u001b[1mDescription:\u001b[22m \u001b[36mGET /price\u001b[39m passes the caller-controlled \u001b[36mreq.query.formula\u001b[39m directly to JavaScript \u001b[36meval\u001b[39m. In this CommonJS module, eva"]
[0.000, "o", "luated expressions can access \u001b[36mprocess\u001b[39m and \u001b[36mrequire\u001b[39m; a token holder can execute code in the server process, for example by invoking \u001b[36mrequire('child_process').execSync(...)\u001b[39m. The route is behind the hardcoded API token in \u001b[36mserver.js:7-12\u001b[39m. Replace expression evaluation with a safe arithmetic parser or accept only validated numeric inputs and compute pricing in fixed code. Static/source-verified; no runtime request was sent because dependencies are absent.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mEvidence:\u001b[22m CWE: CWE-95\r\n\r\nUntrusted query input is executed as JavaScript in the server's module context. CommonJS \u001b[36mrequire\u001b[39m and \u001b[36mprocess\u001b[39m are available to the evaluated code, allowing commands or other code to run with the service process's privileges. Authentication is required by middleware, but the sole token is hardcoded in the same source. No live exploitation was attempted.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequest / Response\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequest:\u001b[22m\r\n    \u001b[2mAuthenticated `GET /price?formula=...` with a JavaScript ex"]
[0.000, "o", "pression such as `require('child_process').execSync('id').toString()` and `x-api-token` equal to the source literal.\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mResponse:\u001b[22m\r\n    \u001b[2m`server.js:24` executes `const total = eval(req.query.formula);` and returns the result. There is no validation or sandbox between the request query and eval.\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mHardcoded API token protects all routes\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n- \u001b[1mWhat an attacker can do:\u001b[22m A person who can read the source or deployment artifact can recover the API credential and pass the middleware protecting every route. The routes expose order data and evaluate pricing input; deployment source exposure and actual data are not established.\r\n- \u001b[1mWho can do it:\u001b[22m any logged-in user\r\n- \u001b[1mWhat they get:\u001b[22m read data they should not be able to read\r\n- \u001b[1mTechnical severity:\u001b[22m high\r\n- \u001b[1mCategory:\u001b[22m hardcoded-secret\r\n- \u001b[1mStatus:\u001b[22m confirmed\r\n- \u001b[1mConfidence:\u001b[22m 95%\r\n- \u001b[1mDescription:\u001b[22m \u001b[36mserver.js\u001b[39m embeds the API bearer token in source and accepts it verbatim from"]
[0.000, "o", " \u001b[36mx-api-token\u001b[39m for every route. Anyone who can read this source or its deployment artifact can recover the credential and authenticate to the API; the token is not loaded from protected runtime configuration or rotated here. Replace it with a required secret supplied through deployment configuration, and rotate this exposed value.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mEvidence:\u001b[22m CWE: CWE-798\r\n\r\nStatic source evidence confirms a credential is committed in code and used as the sole gate for both routes. An attacker with access to the source/artifact can recover it. Whether source is available to an outside attacker in the deployment is not established.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequest / Response\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequest:\u001b[22m\r\n    \u001b[2mRead server.js:7 and server.js:9-12; send `x-api-token: k3Jx9Qw2LpZ8vR5tYb7NcM4dHs6FgA1e` to any route.\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mResponse:\u001b[22m\r\n    \u001b[2mSource defines `const API_TOKEN = 'k3Jx9Qw2LpZ8vR5tYb7NcM4dHs6FgA1e';` and middleware calls `next()` when the request header equals that value; otherwise it returns 401.\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mS"]
[0.000, "o", "QL injection in customer order lookup\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n- \u001b[1mWhat an attacker can do:\u001b[22m A caller passing the route's token can alter the customer predicate and retrieve order rows beyond the requested customer. The code shows order records are returned; their real-world sensitivity and deployment data are unknown.\r\n- \u001b[1mWho can do it:\u001b[22m any logged-in user\r\n- \u001b[1mWhat they get:\u001b[22m read data they should not be able to read\r\n- \u001b[1mTechnical severity:\u001b[22m high\r\n- \u001b[1mCategory:\u001b[22m sql-injection\r\n- \u001b[1mStatus:\u001b[22m confirmed\r\n- \u001b[1mConfidence:\u001b[22m 90%\r\n- \u001b[1mDescription:\u001b[22m \u001b[36mGET /orders\u001b[39m concatenates \u001b[36mreq.query.customer\u001b[39m into a quoted SQL predicate. The only request gate is the static API token in \u001b[36mserver.js:7-12\u001b[39m; a caller with that token can submit a customer value such as \u001b[36m' OR 1=1 -- \u001b[39m and change the predicate to return rows for all customers. Use a bound parameter. No runtime request was sent because the app dependencies are absent.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mEvidence:\u001b[22m CWE: CWE-89\r\n\r\nThe"]
[0.001, "o", " route accepts externally controlled query input and interpolates it into SQL with no validation or binding. This changes the query predicate and can expose all order rows returned by \u001b[36m.all()\u001b[39m. The static token is present in source, but access to deployed source by any given attacker is unverified. Static/source-verified; no HTTP reproduction was run.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequest / Response\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequest:\u001b[22m\r\n    \u001b[2mAuthenticated `GET /orders?customer=%27%20OR%201%3D1%20--%20` with `x-api-token` equal to the source literal.\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mResponse:\u001b[22m\r\n    \u001b[2mAt `server.js:17`, `req.query.customer` is concatenated directly inside `WHERE customer = '…'`; the SQL resulting from that value ends its string literal, adds `OR 1=1`, and comments out the trailing quote.\u001b[22m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "opened 3 of 3 source files\r\n"]
